  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CCASE_Climate Change &amp; Sustainable Energy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aim: Women and marginalised people facing the worst impacts of the climate crises are more resilient to existing and future climate shocks and have enhanced food security. 
Key Target Populations: Rural women, socially excluded people (such as people with disabilities, people living with HIV, people who use drugs, sex workers, LGBTQI populations, young people (people under 35), older people and people marginalised due to their religion or ethnicity), indigenous people, forest-dwelling people and pastoralist communities
Global Outcomes:
&gt; Rural and marginalised people, particularly women transition to climate resilient food systems and collectively organise to support food, energy and income security
&gt;&#xA0;Women and marginalised people design &amp; implement locally-led early warning and early action to reduce loss and damage and increase resilience and food security in the face of climate shocks and stresses 
&gt; Women and marginalised people have increased voice, strengthened agency and leadership to challenge unjust power systems and holders and claim/create space to reduce their vulnerability to loss and damage, climate shocks and build their resilience
&gt;&#xA0;Solidarity with and support to CSO partners strengthens their capacity to hold to account, enhance and support the responsiveness of duty bearers to national climate emergencies 
&gt;&#xA0;A Southern-led, feminist climate justice movement mobilised and strengthened to amplify civil society &amp; grassroots voices to influence and transform national, regional and global agendas and action on climate justice</narrative>
  </description>
